WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:05.250
- We're standin' here at the
Belarusian Ukrainian border.

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:06.720
Here, as you can see,

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.360
the Belarusians have set up barbed wire.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.840
On the other side, just a
few meters away, is Ukraine,

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.793
and they have set up barricades.

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:18.360
The Belarus Ukraine border

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:20.490
has been a strategic location for Russia

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:22.800
since it invaded Ukraine a year ago

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:25.890
when Russian troops
mounted attacks from here.

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:29.940
Now, as Kyiv warned of a
renewed Russian offensive,

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:33.630
tensions along this 620 mile long frontier

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:35.130
are ratchetin' up,

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:37.770
renewing fears in Kyiv and the West

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:41.040
of a possible joint attack on Ukraine.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.320
The Belarusian State Border Committee

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:47.343
invited us on a rare visit
to see what's happening here.

00:00:47.343 --> 00:00:50.843
(speaks foreign language)

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:57.660
In recent weeks along this border,

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:01.080
Belarusian forces have been
holding joint combat drills

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:04.350
with Russian troops,
and on the other side,

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:07.773
Ukraine's military has
been reinforcing defenses.

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:14.010
The Border Patrol says that

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:17.100
there has been a lot of tension
at this particular border,

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:19.140
which is closed at the moment.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:22.053
They say that sometimes drones fly over.

00:01:23.877 --> 00:01:26.220
(drones buzz)

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:29.520
Ukrainian forces have
admitted to such activity

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:32.352
to monitor for potential new attacks.

00:01:32.352 --> 00:01:35.852
(speaks foreign language)

00:01:57.690 --> 00:01:59.250
Guards on the Belarusian side

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:02.280
are keepin' a close eye on the border.

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:06.093
Others are training to intercept
any unauthorized crossings.

00:02:07.205 --> 00:02:10.705
(speaks foreign language)

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:13.800
Belarusian officials say

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.083
they think Ukraine may launch an attack.

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:19.287
Ukraine has dismissed this assertion.

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:23.973
(speaks foreign language)

00:02:36.973 --> 00:02:39.450
Belarusian President Alexander Lukashenko,

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:42.090
an authoritarian ruler and a close ally

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:44.490
of Russian President Vladimir Putin

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:47.910
said in recent days that he
would again let Russian troops

00:02:47.910 --> 00:02:50.670
use Belarus to launch attacks on Ukraine,

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:52.410
but he said he has no intention

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:54.780
of sending his own troops there,

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:58.004
though he warned of one
important exception.

00:02:58.004 --> 00:03:01.504
(speaks foreign language)

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:18.900
Military action would likely come

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:21.720
with challenges for Lukashenko.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.730
Belarus has a small army.

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:26.280
They are not tested, and moreover,

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:30.093
polls show that Belarusians do
not have an appetite for war.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:35.760
But some Belarusians are
supporting Russia in other ways.

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:38.670
Here at the Belarusian Women's Union,

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:41.940
people have been gathering
boxes of donations,

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:46.350
of supplies, food, medicine,
for people in Donbas,

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:49.500
who they say are sufferin'
and need the help.

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:52.290
Vladimir Kazbanov is the Business Manager

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:54.870
of the Alexey Talai Foundation,

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:58.500
where volunteers work to send
supplies to pro-Russian parts

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:01.836
of Ukrainian's Eastern Donbas region.

00:04:01.836 --> 00:04:05.336
(speaks foreign language)

00:04:09.555 --> 00:04:11.070
Kazbanov and his colleagues say

00:04:11.070 --> 00:04:13.170
they try to stay out of politics

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:16.905
and that the suffering of
the war transcends borders.

00:04:16.905 --> 00:04:20.405
(speaks foreign language)

00:04:31.767 --> 00:04:33.540
Lukashenko said that his country

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:38.100
is willing to offer more
assistance to "our Russian brother"

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:40.860
in the war against its
cross border neighbor,

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:44.700
but has dismissed claims by
Kyiv that Putin can pressure him

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:48.129
to take a more direct
role in the conflict.

00:04:48.129 --> 00:04:51.629
(speaks foreign language)

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:00.340
(light music)

